  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between the compound 10,13-dimethyl-17-(5-propan-2-ylhept-5-en-2-yl)-2,3,4,7,8,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-dodecahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-ol and Carboxylesterase 2. This compound is identified as a target of multiple substances, all of which are implicated in the inhibition of Carboxylesterase 2. Specifically, it is a target of Thioredoxin, a protein involved in cellular redox regulation, and is also a target of several other compounds, including 5-Hydroxy-2-Methylchromone-7-O-Rutinoside and (2Alpha,3Beta,17R*,18Beta)-23-O-(Cis-P-Coumaroyl)-19(18->17)-Abeo-28-Norolean-12-Ene-2,3,18-Triol. These targets are known to interact with Carboxylesterase 2, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the inhibition of this enzyme. The evidence is supported by the presence of multiple pathways that converge on Carboxylesterase 2, indicating a plausible and consistent mechanism of action. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that the compound may act as an inhibitor of Carboxylesterase 2 through a common target, Thioredoxin, which is involved in the regulation of enzyme activity.",
